.TH ART 1 "October 2026" "art 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
art \- Arch Linux terminal candy launcher, installer, and preset manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B art
.RI [ --no-splash | --list | --help | --version ]
.br
.B art install
.RI ( --all | CATEGORY | PROGRAM )
.RB [ --dry-run ]
.br
.B art --preset
.I NAME
.br
.B art preset
.RI ( list | "show NAME" | "launch NAME" | "save NAME" )
.RB [ --workspace " N" ]
.RB [ --replace ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Browse a curated catalog of terminal art, install missing programs with pacman,
yay, or paru, and launch them from a fullscreen interface.
Workspace presets support Hyprland's Lua API and Kitty remote control.
.SH KEYS
Arrow keys select programs and categories. Enter launches, slash searches,
F toggles favorites, I installs, R launches randomly, and Esc quits.
A runs an animation sequence, M cycles Matrix effects, S starts a screensaver,
C opens configuration, P opens presets, and U refreshes discovery.
.PP
During automatic playback, Esc, Q, or Ctrl-C stops; Space or Right skips.
In the preset menu, Enter restores and N saves the current workspace.
.SH INSTALLATION
.B art install --all
installs missing catalog packages supported by the available manager.
Pacman-only installations skip AUR entries. Source-only entries are reported
and skipped. Native package-manager confirmation and AUR review remain enabled.
.SH FILES
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/terminal-art-launcher/config.toml
.br
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/terminal-art-launcher/presets/*.json
.PP
XDG_CONFIG_HOME defaults to ~/.config. Presets contain executable command
arguments and should only be imported from trusted sources.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Presets capture one Kitty pane per operating-system window. Spotify's mini-player
must already be open to be repositioned. Screensaver mode does not lock the session.
.SH AUTHORS
Robert Green and contributors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman (8),
.BR kitty (1)
